From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BunkerWeb Windows port <bunkerweb-windows@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] modsecurity-nginx: always use the empty dd() debug macro

nginx for Windows does not define NGX_HAVE_VARIADIC_MACROS, so the non-debug dd() becomes a real function whose
arguments are still compiled, and one of them (clcf) only exists in debug builds. GCC has variadic macros: use the
empty macro unconditionally.

Upstream: none yet, could be proposed to owasp-modsecurity/ModSecurity-nginx (nginx's win32 build lacks the macro)
Check: the native build compiles ngx_http_modsecurity_module.c without this patch

diff --git a/deps/src/modsecurity-nginx/src/ddebug.h b/deps/src/modsecurity-nginx/src/ddebug.h
index 9785421..2c9582c 100644
--- a/deps/src/modsecurity-nginx/src/ddebug.h
+++ b/deps/src/modsecurity-nginx/src/ddebug.h
@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@ static void dd(const char *fmt, ...) {
 
 #else
 
-#   if (NGX_HAVE_VARIADIC_MACROS)
+#   if 1 /* Windows port: NGX_HAVE_VARIADIC_MACROS is not defined on win32 */
 
 #       define dd(...)
 
